[[ ## document ## ]]
{
  "title": "CAM Stakeholder Call — Tuesday 10:00 AM",
  "path": "engagements/stonebridge/cam/2025/call-materials/cam-stakeholder-call-materials.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "CAM Stakeholder Call — Tuesday 10:00 AM (90 minutes)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Prepared by Lucia Mendes, Senior Accountant. Participants: Gabriel (CAM lead), Evan (client), Lucia (tax). Objective: resolve two disputed line items, confirm allocation logic, and align on settlement path. All materials below are ready for the call."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "1. Meeting Logistics & Commitments"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Call confirmed: Tuesday 10:00 AM – 11:30 AM (90-minute block).",
          "Lucia will bring the signed acknowledgment of scope and deliverables.",
          "Side-by-side breakdown of the two disputed line items (detailed in Section 2).",
          "Vendor and allocation documentation package (vendor invoices, allocation schedules, K-1 allocation logic).",
          "Thursday delivery: revised reconciliation and settlement draft, conditional on agreement reached on Tuesday."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "2. Disputed Line Items — Side-by-Side Breakdown"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The two disputed items are: (A) Management fee allocation — specifically the 60/40 split vs. 50/50; and (B) Vendor setup costs (Cardinal Ridge PBC hold). Each line item is shown with the client's position, the firm's position, and the supporting documentation."
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Line Item", "Client Position (Evan)", "Firm Position (CAM/Gabriel)", "Supporting Docs"],
        "rows": [
          ["A: Management fee allocation", "50/50 split per verbal agreement at inception (Q1 2024).", "60/40 split per signed engagement letter (Section 4.2) and board-approved fee schedule.", "Signed engagement letter (p. 12); board minutes (Feb 2024); email from Gabriel (Mar 2024)."],
          ["B: Vendor setup costs — Cardinal Ridge PBC", "Costs should be allocated to CAM's overhead, not client share.", "Costs are pass-through per vendor agreement; allocation to client is standard; hold until Rosalind signs off on the fee.", "Vendor agreement (Cardinal Ridge, p. 3); fee sign-off memo (draft, pending Rosalind); allocation schedule (v. 2)."]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. K-1 Allocation Logic Documentation"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The K-1 allocation logic used for the disputed items is documented below, for reference on the call. This matches the signed acknowledgment and the vendor/allocation package."
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          "Management fee: allocated based on ownership percentages as of the last day of the tax year. For FY2024, ownership was 60% CAM / 40% outside investor group. The 50/50 split would require an amended operating agreement, which has not been executed.",
          "Vendor setup costs: allocated pro-rata to the benefit received. Cardinal Ridge PBC costs are directly attributable to the client's new line of business, so 100% of those costs are allocated to the client, subject to Rosalind's fee sign-off (hold in place).",
          "Allocation methodology is documented in the K-1 workpaper (v. 2, attached) and cross-referenced to the partnership agreement (Article VII)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Dispute Resolution Framework"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The following framework is proposed to guide Tuesday's discussion and, if alignment is reached, the Thursday deliverable."
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Both parties present their position on each disputed line item (10 minutes each, per item).",
          "Review supporting documentation side-by-side — no new documents introduced after the call.",
          "Identify the single governing document for each dispute (engagement letter for Item A; vendor agreement for Item B).",
          "If governing document is unambiguous, adopt its terms; if ambiguous, escalate to the fallback (see step 5).",
          "Fallback: 50/50 cost sharing for Item A if the operating agreement is amended retroactively (executed by Friday); for Item B, defer allocation until Rosalind signs off, then apply standard pass-through.",
          "Document any agreed resolution in the Thursday revised reconciliation and settlement draft; both Gabriel and Evan sign off by Friday close."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "5. Deliverables & Next Steps"
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Item", "Due", "Owner", "Status"],
        "rows": [
          ["Signed acknowledgment", "Tuesday (bring to call)", "Lucia", "Ready"],
          ["Side-by-side breakdown", "Tuesday (bring to call)", "Lucia", "Ready"],
          ["Vendor/allocation docs", "Tuesday (bring to call)", "Lucia", "Ready"],
          ["Revised reconciliation", "Thursday", "Lucia (with Gabriel's input)", "Pending agreement"],
          ["Settlement draft", "Thursday", "Lucia (with Evan's input)", "Pending agreement"],
          ["Cardinal Ridge PBC hold", "On hold until Rosalind sign-off", "Lucia / Rosalind", "In progress"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "If agreement is reached on Tuesday, the revised reconciliation and settlement draft will be delivered Thursday, with final sign-off by Friday. If no agreement is reached, the hold on Cardinal Ridge PBC remains, and a follow-up call will be scheduled within five business days."
      }
    ]
  }
}
